<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">2000 Summer Olympics</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/2000">2000</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a> · Also known as Sydney 2000 Olympics</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The 2000 Summer Olympics were held in Sydney, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a>, from 15 September to 1 October 2000, with about 10,000 athletes from 199 national Olympic committees. Remembered for their organisation and atmosphere, they included Cathy Freeman, an Aboriginal athlete who lit the cauldron, winning the 400 metres. They were the second Summer Games held in Australia, after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/melbourne">Melbourne</a> in 1956.</p></div>
